WEBVTT

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.416
COMMITTEE ON CALIFORNIA, MEXICO

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:19.319
COLLABORATION AND DIALOG. IT'S

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.855
MY HONOR TO CHAIR THAT

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.956
COMMITTEE. WE MAY HAVE SOME

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:25.859
COLLEAGUES OF MINE IN THE SENATE

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.394
BREEZING IN AND OUT DURING THIS

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.428
INFORMATIONAL HEARING. I HOPE

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.562
YOU'LL BEAR WITH US. IT'S AN

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:30.563
INTERESTING TIME IN THE CAPITOL

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.099
RIGHT NOW WITH FOLKS IN AND OUT,

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.568
SO I'M LOOKING FORWARD TO THIS

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.603
CONVERSATION AND HEARING FROM

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:37.771
SOME OF OUR ESTEEMED PANELISTS.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.773
I THINK AS MANY OF YOU KNOW, WE

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.508
HAVE A UNIQUE, OVERLAPPING,

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.411
INTERDEPENDENT, SHARED HISTORY

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.545
BETWEEN THE STATE AND BETWEEN

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.714
MEXICO. AND IT'S INTERTWINED IN

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:48.715
CURRENT EVENTS, I THINK PREVENT

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.751
PRESENT US A UNIQUE OPPORTUNITY

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:52.952
TO DEVELOP AN AGENDA THAT CAN

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.220
TAKE INTO CONSIDERATION AND

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.389
BRING INTO FOCUS LONG OVERDUE

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.023
REPRESENTATION AND PARTICIPATION

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.460
ON GENDER. IN MEXICO, WE HAVE

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.462
THE HISTORIC ELECTION OF THE

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:03.696
FIRST WOMAN PRESIDENT, PRESIDENT

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.398
ELECT CLAUDIA SHEINBAUM. THE

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.368
RECENT ANNOUNCEMENT OF THE

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.402
NOMINATION OF VICE PRESIDENT

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.571
KAMALA HARRIS AS A STANDARD

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:12.639
BEARER FOR A MAJOR POLITICAL

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.107
PARTY IN THE UNITED STATES,

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.074
FORMER SENATOR AND ATTORNEY

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.010
GENERAL OF THE STATE OF

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:18.011
CALIFORNIA AND ADDITION IN

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.413
CALIFORNIA. WE HAVE A NUMBER OF

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.414
DISTINGUISHED WOMEN LEADERS IN

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.183
THE RACE TO BE THE NEXT GOVERNOR

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.584
OF CALIFORNIA IN THE 2026

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.152
ELECTION. IN OUR HISTORIES,

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:29.055
COLLIDE AND COINCIDE IN WAYS

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.056
THAT CAN ALLOW FOR THE

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.558
DEVELOPMENT OF AN AGENDA

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.625
CENTERED AROUND GENDER EQUITY

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.061
AND GENDER REPRESENTATION. BUT

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.630
BUILDING THIS AGENDA AND

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:40.400
PROVIDING THIS PERSPECTIVE AND

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.601
FOCUS DOES NOT HAPPEN OVERNIGHT.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.636
WITHOUT APPROPRIATE DIALOG

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:46.139
UNDERSTANDING AND POLICY

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.140
MECHANISMS. MEXICO, FOR THE

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:49.075
FIRST TIME, IS REQUIRING

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.109
AFFIRMATIVE ACTION POLICIES FOR

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.111
FEDERAL, SENATORIAL POSITIONS,

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.012
REQUIRING THAT POLITICAL LEADERS

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.814
NOMINATE PEOPLE FROM

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:55.348
MARGINALIZED COMMUNITIES,

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:58.084
INCLUDING MIGRANTS, INDIGENOUS,

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.018
AFRO-AMERICAN, AND PEOPLE WHO

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.120
IDENTIFY AS LGBTQ AND THOSE THAT

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.755
LIVE WITH DISABILITIES. IN 2019,

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.892
CONSTITUTIONAL REFORMS REQUIRED

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:06.759
BALANCED REPRESENTATION OF WOMEN

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.596
AND MEN IN CANDIDACIES AND

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.397
POSITIONS IN THE EXECUTIVE,

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:11.931
LEGISLATIVE, AND JUDICIAL

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.000
BRANCHES OF GOVERNMENT. ALTHOUGH

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.001
CALIFORNIA AND MEXICO HAVE MADE

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.437
GREAT STRIDES IN THE FIGHT FOR

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:19.806
GENDER EQUALITY, EQUITY AND

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:20.707
REPRESENTATION, BUILDING AN

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.642
AGENDA CENTERED AROUND THIS THAT

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:25.178
CROSSES BORDERS AND BLENDED

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.881
CULTURES WILL REQUIRE A DEEPER

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:28.882
UNDERSTANDING OF THE UNIQUE

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.150
LEGAL AND POLITICAL ASPECTS OF

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.318
BOTH OUR GOVERNMENTS AND OUR

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.153
PEOPLES, AS WELL AS A DEEPENING

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.054
UNDERSTANDING OF THE

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.923
OPPORTUNITIES BEFORE US TO

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.192
DEVELOP A SHARED AGENDA. TODAY

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.493
IS THE 15TH ANNIVERSARY OF THE

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.830
CALIFORNIA MEXICO ADVOCACY DAY,

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.098
AND FOR 15 YEARS THIS COMMITTEE

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:47.267
HAS INVESTIGATED NUMEROUS ISSUES

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.068
AFFECTING OUR SHARED

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.204
CONSTITUENCIES. ON THE 15TH

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.006
ANNIVERSARY, IT IS FITTING THAT

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.240
THE SENATE SELECT COMMITTEE ON

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.709
CALIFORNIA COOPERATION AND

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:57.176
DIALOG EXPLORE UNIQUE

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.946
OPPORTUNITIES TO BUILD AN AGENDA

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:00.914
WITH A GENDER PERSPECTIVE

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.649
THROUGH BILATERAL COOPERATION

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:03.750
BETWEEN OUR TWO COUNTRIES. SO

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.618
TODAY, WE'RE GOING TO HEAR FROM

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.619
SOME DISTINGUISHED EXPERTS AND

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.721
REPRESENTATIVES WHO PROVIDE

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:09.656
THEIR PERSPECTIVE ON HOW

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.258
CALIFORNIA AND MEXICO CAN BUILD

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:15.161
AN AGENDA CENTERED AROUND TAKING

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:16.095
INTO ACCOUNT AND THE

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:18.231
PERSPECTIVES AROUND GENDER.

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:20.767
UNFORTUNATELY, TWO OF OUR

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.602
PANELISTS WILL NOT BE ABLE TO

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:23.570
MAKE IT TODAY BECAUSE OF

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.571
ILLNESS. AND WE WISH THE

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.773
GOVERNOR OF SONORA AND THE

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:27.807
COMMISSIONER, GARCIA BAUER, BOTH

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:30.310
A SPEEDY RECOVERY. DARCY TROTMAN

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.045
WILL PROVIDE A FEW REMARKS ON

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.780
BEHALF OF THE COMMISSION ON THE

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.648
STATUS OF WOMEN AND GIRLS. BUT

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:36.783
BEFORE DOING SO, I'D LIKE TO

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.518
GIVE OUR ESTEEMED CONSUL GENERAL

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.619
OF MEXICO IN SACRAMENTO A

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.121
TREASURED PARTNER TO THIS

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.923
COMMITTEE, TO MYSELF AND TO THE

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:44.958
SENATE ON CALIFORNIA, MEXICO

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:48.628
ADVOCACY DAY TODAY AND BEYOND,

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.430
CONSUL CHRISTIAN GONZALEZ TO

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.631
SHARE A FEW WORDS. CONSUL,

00:03:51.698 --> 00:04:02.875
WELCOME.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:15.922
SENORA.

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:18.958
MUY BUENAS TARDES. A GRACIAS,

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:22.095
STEVE. MY DEAR FRIEND. AMIGO A

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.897
VERY STRONG ALLY TO THE

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:28.101
GOVERNMENT OF MEXICO, GOOD

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.104
AFTERNOON, EVERYONE. IT'S A TRUE

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.271
PRIVILEGE TO BE HERE WITH ALL OF

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:35.008
YOU TODAY. TODAY, TO BE PART OF

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.076
THIS IMPORTANT ANNUAL EVENT. AT

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:41.114
THE OUTSET, I WANT TO EXPRESS MY

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.082
DEEP GRATITUDE TO ALL OF THOSE

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.183
PRESENT, AS WELL AS TO OUR

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.819
PARTNERS IN THE SELECT COMMITTEE

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:47.787
FOR THE MEXICO, CALIFORNIA

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:48.921
COOPERATION AND DIALOG IN THE

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:51.491
CALIFORNIA SENATE. YOUR

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:52.492
COMMITMENT AND DEDICATION HAVE

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:54.594
BEEN CRUCIAL TO THE ONGOING

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.662
SUCCESS OF THIS DIALOG, WHICH

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.697
NOT ONLY STRENGTHENS OUR

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:58.765
ECONOMIC AND CULTURAL TIES, BUT

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.566
ALSO DRIVES JOINT INITIATIVES

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.369
THAT BENEFIT OUR COMMUNITIES.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:06.773
FOR 15 YEARS, AS SENATOR PADILLA

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:07.807
HAVE MENTIONED, ADVOCACY DAY HAS

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:10.543
BEEN A KEY FOR STRENGTHENING THE

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:12.979
BONDS BETWEEN MEXICO DIALOG AND

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:16.049
ISSUES THAT DEEPLY AFFECT BOTH

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:17.183
SIDES OF THE BORDER. OVER THE

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.986
YEARS, THIS EVENT HAS SERVED AS

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.688
A FORUM FOR COLLABORATION AND

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.657
MUTUAL UNDERSTANDING BETWEEN OUR

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:25.858
NATIONS, AND IT HAS ALLOWED US

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.527
NOT TO ONLY REINFORCE COMMERCIAL

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.996
AND ECONOMIC CONNECTIONS, BUT

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:33.199
ALSO DEEPEN OUR COOPERATION IN

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:37.770
CRITICAL AREAS SUCH AS EDUCATION,

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.339
ENVIRONMENT AND MIGRATION.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:41.441
THANKS TO THIS FORUM, WE HAVE

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.409
BEEN ABLE TO IDENTIFY

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:43.943
OPPORTUNITIES AND PROPOSE

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.746
CONCRETE RECOMMENDATIONS FOR

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:47.780
PUBLIC POLICIES THAT BENEFIT

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.382
BOTH SIDES OF THE BORDER. THIS

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:52.151
YEAR, WE ARE INTENTIONALLY

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.186
FOCUSING ON THE DEVELOPMENT OF

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.288
AN INCLUSIVE GENDER AGENDA

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:58.257
THROUGH COLLABORATION BETWEEN

00:05:58.324 --> 00:05:59.225
MEXICO AND CALIFORNIA. THIS

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:01.427
APPROACH ADDRESSES THE CURRENT

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:04.263
CONTEXT AND UNDERSCORES OUR

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.431
COMMITMENT TO A FEMINIST FOREIGN

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:08.501
POLICY THAT PROMOTES EQUITY AND

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:10.703
INCLUSION IN ALL ASPECTS OF OUR

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.906
SOCIETIES. IT IS CRUCIAL TO

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.675
HIGHLIGHT THAT THE CHOICE OF

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:17.410
THIS THEME COULD NOT BE

00:06:17.477 --> 00:06:19.479
APPROPRIATE, ESPECIALLY IF IT'S

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.147
NOT BECAUSE, AS YOU MENTIONED,

00:06:21.214 --> 00:06:22.949
SENATOR PADILLA, THE ELECTION OF

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:24.951
THE PRESIDENT OF MEXICO, OF

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:28.154
DOCTOR DOCTOR CLAUDIA SHEINBAUM,

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.188
HER NEAR INAUGURATION TO THE

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:31.057
PRESIDENCY NOT ONLY WILL

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:33.659
RECOGNIZE THE POTENTIAL OF

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:36.362
FEMALE PARTICIPATION IN POLITICS

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:39.599
AND SOCIETY, BUT ALSO MARKS A

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.068
HISTORICAL MILESTONE AS THE

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:44.904
FIRST WOMAN LEADER TO ASSUME THE

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.105
PRESIDENCY IN ALL OF THE NORTH

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:51.010
AMERICAN REGION. HER EXEMPLARY

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:51.978
LEADERSHIP IN MEXICO CITY HAS

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:55.014
NOT ONLY INSPIRED MANY OF US,

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:57.316
BUT ALSO DEMONSTRATES HOW WOMEN

00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:00.453
CAN LEAD CHANGE PARADIGMS AND

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.387
STRENGTHEN FEMALE REPRESENTATION

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:04.657
GLOBALLY TO INVIGORATE AND BUILD

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:06.959
A MORE DYNAMIC AND MEANINGFUL

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:09.095
COOPERATION BETWEEN MEXICO AND

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:12.331
CALIFORNIA, IT IS ESSENTIAL TO

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:13.332
IDENTIFY AREAS OF COLLABORATION,

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.835
SUCH AS THE EXCHANGE OF BEST

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:18.504
PRACTICES IN PUBLIC POLICY,

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:18.971
ORGANIZING SUMMITS AND

00:07:19.038 --> 00:07:21.774
CONFERENCES ON GENDER EQUALITY,

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:22.875
AND CREATING JOINT PROGRAMS THAT

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.177
PROMOTE EDUCATION AND ECONOMICAL

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:27.280
EMPOWERMENT OF WOMEN. WE ALSO

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:30.283
EMPHASIZE THE IMPORTANCE OF THE

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:31.250
MEMORANDUM OF UNDERSTANDING

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:33.186
BETWEEN THE MEXICAN SECRETARY OF

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:35.755
FOREIGN AFFAIRS AND THE

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:36.789
CALIFORNIA COMMISSION OF THE

00:07:36.856 --> 00:07:38.491
STATUS OF WOMEN AND GIRLS. THIS

00:07:38.558 --> 00:07:41.427
ROBUST AND ACTIVE AGREEMENT

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:42.562
ADDRESSES ISSUES SUCH AS GENDER

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:45.431
BASED VIOLENCE, PAY GAPS, AND

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:47.867
UNEQUAL ACCESS TO RESOURCES AND

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:50.636
OPPORTUNITIES. IT REPRESENTS A

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:51.604
CRUCIAL STARTING POINT FOR

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:53.639
DRIVING BORDER ACTIONS THAT

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:56.509
BENEFITS THE MOST VULNERABLE

00:07:56.576 --> 00:07:59.445
COMMUNITIES, INCLUDING MEXICAN

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:00.446
AND INDIGENOUS WOMEN, RURAL

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:02.715
WOMEN, WOMEN WITH DISABILITIES

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:05.785
AND LGBTQ PLUS COMMUNITY.

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:08.621
BILATERAL COOPERATION BETWEEN

00:08:08.688 --> 00:08:09.522
MEXICO AND CALIFORNIA CAN

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:11.557
GREATLY BENEFIT FROM ADOPTING

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:13.459
GENDER SENSITIVE PRINCIPLES AND

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:16.829
PROPOSALS. BOTH REGIONS SHARE

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:19.599
FUNDAMENTAL VALUES SUCH AS

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:20.099
EQUALITY, DIVERSITY AND

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:22.535
INCLUSION, POSITIONING US TO

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:24.704
LEAD SIMILAR AGENDAS ON

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.705
INTERNATIONAL LEVEL BY WORKING

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:28.341
TOGETHER, MEXICO AND CALIFORNIA

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:29.242
NOT ONLY FOSTER MORE

00:08:29.308 --> 00:08:31.344
COMPREHENSIVE AND EQUITABLE

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.411
POLICIES, BUT ALSO SERVE AS A

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.714
MODEL OF INTERNATIONAL

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.316
COOPERATION IN PROMOTING SOCIAL

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:40.086
JUSTICE, JUSTICE AND PARITY. THE

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:41.153
SYNERGY BETWEEN OUR REGIONS CAN

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.422
RESULT IN A SIGNIFICANT IMPACT,

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.825
CREATING MORE JUST AND EQUITABLE

00:08:45.892 --> 00:08:48.861
SOCIETIES WHERE ALL WOMEN HAVE

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:51.764
THE OPPORTUNITY TO THRIVE. ON

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:52.832
BEHALF OF THE GOVERNMENT OF

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:54.567
MEXICO, I SINCERELY THANK THE

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:55.067
CALIFORNIA SENATE SELECT

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:57.603
COMMITTEE, PARTICULARLY TO AGAIN

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:00.306
TO OUR FRIEND, SENATOR STEVE

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:03.442
PADILLA AND ALL HIS HIS HARD

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:06.045
WORK THAT HAVE ALLOWED US TO NOW

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:09.181
CREATE THIS IMPORTANT DIALOG, AS

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:10.416
WELL AS THE CALIFORNIA CHAMBER

00:09:10.483 --> 00:09:12.618
OF COMMERCE FOR THEIR PRESENCE

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:13.619
AND COMMITMENT TO THIS SHARED

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.821
CAUSE. MAY THIS 50TH ANNIVERSARY

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:17.590
OF MEXICO DAY AT THE CAPITOL BE

00:09:17.657 --> 00:09:18.691
A RESOUNDING SUCCESS AND

00:09:18.758 --> 00:09:21.360
STARTING POINT FOR AN EVEN

00:09:21.427 --> 00:09:24.163
BRIGHTER AND MORE COLLABORATIVE

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.332
FUTURE BETWEEN OUR GREAT NATIONS.

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:27.466
SIN DUDA, ESTO ES TIEMPO DE

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:30.670
MUJERES. ES TIEMPO DE MINORIAS

00:09:30.736 --> 00:09:32.905
ES TIEMPO DE MIGRANTES Y ES

00:09:32.972 --> 00:09:34.040
TIEMPO DE CONSTRUIR UNA

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:35.041
SOCIEDAD. UNA COMUNIDAD MAS

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:36.609
FUERTE PARA TODOS PARA TODOS Y

00:09:36.676 --> 00:09:39.478
PARA TODOS. FELIZ FELIZ DIA DE

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:42.281
MEXICO EN CALIFORNIA Y QUÊ. VIVA

